{"name":"Carefree","hex":"#dce9e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carefree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without cares or worries; free of concern or worries; without difficulty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carefree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carefree, Arizona","blocks":[{"text":"Carefree is a town in Maricopa County, Arizona, United States. It is located north of both Phoenix and Scottsdale in the far northeast area of the Phoenix metropolitan area. As of the 2020 United States census, the population of the town was 3,690."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Carefree-_Carefree_Town_Marker.JPG/330px-Carefree-_Carefree_Town_Marker.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carefree%2C_Arizona"},{"title":"Carefree (chant)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Carefree\" is a football chant sung by supporters of Chelsea Football Club, and it is meant to demonstrate indifference, valour and possibly belligerence when in an alien and hostile environment. The original tune is \"Lord of the Dance”."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carefree_(chant)"},{"title":"Carefree (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Carefree is a 1938 American musical romantic comedy film directed by Mark Sandrich and starring Fred Astaire, Ginger Rogers, and Ralph Bellamy. With a plot similar to screwball comedies of the period, Carefree is the shortest of the Astaire–Rogers films, featuring only four musical numbers. Carefree is often remembered as the film in which Astaire and Rogers shared a long on-screen kiss at the conclusion of their dance to \"I Used to Be Color Blind\"; all previous kisses having been either quick pecks or simply implied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Carefree_%281938_film_poster%29.png/330px-Carefree_%281938_film_poster%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carefree_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Carefreeaz_seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Carefreeaz_seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarefreeaz_seal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Carefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG/500px-Carefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Carefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG/1280px-Carefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Carefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG/500px-Carefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Carefree Town Hall located at 8 East Sundial Circle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarefree-Carefree_Town_Hall.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Carefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG/500px-Carefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Carefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG/1280px-Carefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Carefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG/500px-Carefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Carefree Sundial","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarefree-Carefree_Sundial-1959.JPG"}],"sounds":{"carefree":[{"ty